Here's an update on my wizard ...

I tried donating twice to a priest for more AC.  Didn't work.  On Dlvl
30 I ran across the corpse of my archaeologist who died from choking
on a lizard corpse.  He had lots of useful stuff I could've used like
speed boots, helm of brilliance, and gauntlets of dexterity. 
Unfortunately I had already used three wishes from the WoW in the
castle to get those.  The ring of protection also came from the bones
file.  I wasted the charges on my magic markers by alternately writing
cursed and blessed scrolls of enchant armor to try to get my gauntlets
of dexterity up to +5 ... to no avail.  Two of the empty magic markers
are from the bones file, but I figure I might as well keep them
around.  I also got the magic lamp from the bones file.

On Dlvl 20 I have a chest full of spellbooks, another luckstone, and a
secondary Bag of Holding.  I'm thinking what I'll do for now is keep
#offering and #praying until I get a spellbook of polymorph.  Then, I
can use that to polypile lots of stuff and get more magic markers.

Also, what should I use my three WoW wishes for?  Magic markers?  A
spellbook of polymorph?  I'm thinking I might just wish for the
spellbook ... I have a complete kit of armor, so the wishes aren't
good for much.  Besides, it might take a lot more sacrificing and
offering to get that spellbook.

Also, pretty the only conduct I've kept throughout the whole game has
been one I made up on my own: pick-axe-less.  I've never used a
pick-axe.  That makes those wands of digging that I come across
especially useful.  But Gehennom with magic mapping isn't as bad as
Gehennom with a pick-axe but no magic mapping.

